From b1d06cd21fb765ad6560939f93abcad94585ae83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dixonSolutions <203963471+dixonSolutions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:24:28 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] main: Add a dual payload mode (CHAINLOAD)

Embed a second payload, an arm64 Image such as U-Boot, next to Linux.
New board hooks decide which one boots: chain_select() fills in the reset
status and keys and may ask for the embedded Linux, chain_arm() and
fallback_arm() run right before either jump.

For the chained image uniLoader copies the previous bootloader's FDT
(if valid, else the embedded DTB) to CHAINLOAD_FDT_ADDR and the image to
CHAINLOAD_ENTRY, and jumps with x0 = FDT. The decision, reset status, keys,
FDT address and androidboot.bootloader/revision are kept in a record at
CHAINLOAD_HANDOFF_ADDR for the next OS. CHAINLOAD_DEFAULT=1/2 force the
fallback (2 with the board watchdog armed) for testing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
